 under Wagner's guidelines, the state may be eligible for $1 billion to $1.=
5 billion.  "Certainly to the extent that it helped refute what California =
has been saying, it's a victory," Bailey said of the judge's statement.  Bu=
t Davis said the nation's big power sellers never came to the table with a =
serious offer.  "Not surprisingly, the energy pirates that bilked ratepayer=
s out of billions of dollars stonewalled and refused to negotiate in good f=
aith," Davis said.  $716 MILLION OFFER  Wagner disclosed yesterday that the=
