rge profits, the generators said.  "The refunds sought by California would =
send a profoundly counterproductive message to suppliers: when prices are l=
ow and surpluses exist, you face a steep downside; when scarcity develops a=
nd prices rise we will take away all upside [profit]. No one will invest [i=
n California power facilities] in that climate," the generators' statement =
said. "The power supply shortage thus will continue without relief."   http=
