od, he said, although far shy of the more than $375 million California soug=
ht from Reliant.  Mr. Wagner said the industry offered a total of $716 mill=
ion to settle the matter.  The refund issue is fast becoming a test of the =
agency's authority and credibility. The FERC, a onetime regulatory backwate=
r, has come under intense scrutiny of late for its largely hands-off monito=
ring of deregulated California markets. The commission has ordered some com=
panies to pay refunds, but they have been relatively small -- such as a $12=
4 million rebate covering wholesale electricity bills in California in Janu=
ary and February.  California Gov. Gray Davis has said he hopes two new FER=
C members will take a much more aggressive tack. The agency is expected to =
